NAME
    cmp - compare two files byte for byte

SYNOPSIS
    cmp file1 file2

DESCRIPTION
    Compares the two files. When they are identical cmp prints nothing.
    Otherwise it reports the first difference (N and M count from 1):

        cmp: files differ: byte N, line M

    or, when one file is a prefix of the other, the one that ended
    first:

        cmp: EOF on file1        (file2 is longer)
        cmp: EOF on file2        (file1 is longer)

    Both files are streamed side by side through two read handles.
    Errors: "cmp: file1 not found", "cmp: file2 not found". cmp is
    /BIN/CMP.

LIMITS
    None beyond the OS's: a file over 64K cannot be opened.

EXAMPLES
    cmp /FRUIT.TXT /FRUIT2.TXT   cmp: files differ: byte 55, line 5
    cmp /FRUIT.TXT FRUIT.TXT     silent (in /, the same file)

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: the 8K limit on file1, which the P8X
    read into memory because its BIOS had one read stream.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/cmp.c 2026-09-23.

